      "writtenOn": "2025-03-20T00:07:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think similar extraction during exceution would require some additional information. Unlike `extract_apks` where all apks are `PRESIGNED`, the apps in the prebuilt shim apexes (companinon CL in this topic) should be written as\n```\nname\u003d\"CtsShim.apk\" certificate\u003d\"build/make/target/product/security/testkey.x509.pem\" private_key\u003d\"build/make/target/product/security/testkey.pk8\" partition\u003d\"system\"\n```\n\nDuring execution, we would be able to determine that `CtsShim.apk` is an apk-in-apex, but we would not know its test certificates.\n\nHowever, I do agree that this can lead to signing issues if users do not declare the apps explicitly. As an alternative, WDYT about creating a validation action for prebuilt_apexes that deapexes them and checks that if there any .apks, they must be declared in `Apps`?",
      "parentUuid": "e11be762_eb3ea7e0",
      "revId": "3778add0753f1dbe293b2026fb15d7c959df5d07",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
